## Proposed outputs and target identity

Require six precision records: each of two named interventions times survival_day42, admission_by_day42 and alive_outpatient_day42. Unit is **probability**, range[0,1], not percentage points. Each record binds exact estimand/action/population or observed-history hash/horizon/continuation/support/DGP/cell, truth-method/version, protocol/source/seed keys, roster and batch hashes, full allocated total, numerator, independent-unit definition/count, point estimate, MCSE, numerical allowances, interval method/limits, matched-pilot reference/SE and status/reason. These are evaluator-only metadata composed with the existing vector, not an added learner predictor. A versioned companion contract is preferable to silently changing the meaning of legacy wire fields; final schema mechanics belong to the bounded interface implementation after acceptance.

For unconditional marginal evaluation, each complete independent patient continuation contributes one indicator per event per arm. Death remains in all event denominators. Admission means ever admitted by42days, including an admission preceding subsequent death; alive/outpatient is the day42state, not one minus ever-admission. Event times, complete arm rosters and paired IDs remain retained. Missing event ascertainment, failed paths or lost rows are errors/unresolved, never zeros or removed complete cases. Check alive/outpatient <= survival; do not force these three overlapping probabilities to sum to one. Retain within-arm and cross-arm covariance/paired batch identities. This proposal admits per-arm marginals; it does not invent an overall score or a probability contrast consumer. Any later named contrast needs its own paired uncertainty and matched precision binding.

Conditional ISI retains each arm's own alive/outpatient numerator count out of the complete roster, its ISI mean and ratio/sample-mean uncertainty. Its .05 ISI and matched-SE rules, accepted conditional approximation checks, existing contrast requirements and source-calibration criteria remain unchanged. Never substitute a probability tolerance or probability pilot for symptom precision. A mathematically established zero conditioning probability makes the symptom target undefined; zero sampled eligible paths means the numerical symptom estimate is undefined **and acceptance unresolved**, with reason `no_sampled_eligible_paths`, unless independent analytic evidence establishes structural zero. Zero total paths is missing execution, not probability zero. A required full vector cannot become accepted merely because its available components pass; genuinely undefined symptom targets must be accompanied by established-zero evidence.

## Proposed probability precision gate and budgets

The new absolute component MCSE maximum is **0.001 probability units** (0.1percentage point), explicitly a provisional engineering choice. Rationale: keeps numerical noise well below display-scale differences and uses the same order as the already accepted reduced probability checks without claiming those checks mandated this value. For each component let `epsilon = min(0.001, 0.1 * S_min)` using the accepted probability pilot below. Require numerical MCSE <=epsilon and all applicable conditional numerical allowances within epsilon. No relative-error-to-p rule is introduced: rare events do not justify dividing by p-hat or fabricating an SE floor.

Keep10,000 paired continuation draws per outer batch and maximum1,000 independent batches (10million paired draws), as in the G1 plan. Begin assessment after32 independent batches; record all attempted batches and their independent seed identities. For scalar batch estimates q_b, report mean(q_b), sample SD(q_b)/sqrt(B), and the corresponding covariance matrix across six components. Equal batch size is required; unequal/incomplete batches are unresolved unless a separately reviewed estimator is used. Paired draws are not twice the independent sample size. Conditional batches must independently regenerate posterior filters as already required; repeat descendants of a fixed filter are not independent outer batches. Batch MCSE measures sampling variation, not particle/quadrature bias.

Extend the existing conditional numerical budget to each probability component with its own epsilon: epsilon/4 for quadrature change, epsilon/4 for particle refinement discrepancy, epsilon/4 for within-filter rollout MCSE, epsilon/4 for between-filter integration MCSE; retain the total-MCSE gate. Apply the accepted two successive refinements' absolute change plus1.96paired MCSE rule at epsilon/4, particle levels1,024/4,096/16,384/65,536 and32independent filters/level. No larger cap, fixed-filter averaging substitute or new algorithm. The budget is an empirical numerical-stability rule, not a certified posterior bias bound. Pilot refinement and truth refinement must agree on the same information set and final numerical level. Reduced checks and deliberately omitted-factor faults remain mandatory.

For IID Bernoulli marginal draws also retain the raw pooled binomial MCSE and95%Wilson interval, and diagnose material disagreement with outer-batch uncertainty rather than selecting the smaller number. For zero events report exact one-sided95%upper bound `1 - 0.05^(1/N)`; for all events the complementary exact lower bound. Those formulas apply only to genuinely independent Bernoulli units. For correlated conditional/filter descendants report independent outer-batch uncertainty; do not apply Wilson/exact binomial limits with descendant count N. If all independent batches have zero event counts, a valid conservative bound uses the B independent batch indicators of any event: marginal event probability <= probability(any event in a batch), whose upper bound is `1 - 0.05^(1/B)`; analogous complement for all-success. This bound is deliberately loose, labeled as such, and generally leaves the conditional rare component unresolved at the cap. Do not replace B with the number of descendants.

A numerical zero MCSE is not an analytic truth certificate. Boundary or otherwise degenerate empirical sampling variation requires either a valid independent uncertainty bound no larger than epsilon and a positive matched-pilot binding, or analytic/enumerated structural evidence; otherwise unresolved. Analytic/enumerated zero/one probabilities require an independently verified structural/event enumeration derivation and no unreported numerical integration. Known death at cutoff can give structural survival/alive-outpatient zero but does not by itself determine past admission-by42status without the required event history. Finite quadrature alone remains numerical with its error assessment.

Intervals/bounds are precision diagnostics at the retained stopping point. Optional stopping and six components do not turn their nominal95%intervals into simultaneous/sequential coverage guarantees; this proposal makes no such guarantee. All six gates must pass separately. Cap exhaustion, missing pilot, unresolved approximation, invalid/nonfinite estimate or inadequate independent units yields explicit `unresolved`, not `computed` or analytic. Valid partial outputs remain retained with per-component status; no overall winner is emitted.

## Probability-specific matched pilot: explicit proposed exception

**This subsection is a proposed narrow addition/exception, not a reinterpretation of the accepted per-trial-minimum rule.** That rule remains unchanged for ISI, quality, source-shift calibration and their existing comparisons. Applying a minimum of every individual plug-in Bernoulli SE to probabilities routinely returns zero for finite rare-event arms even when the estimator's actual sampling variance is positive. A positive replacement constant would be unjustified. Instead, estimate the matched sampling uncertainty directly from the required independent trials.

Run1,000 independent randomized comparison trials for each required n/configuration/history, in the existing disjoint pilot namespace, retaining every trial and its complete arm roster, event indicators, counts, arm-mean probabilities and seeds. Use actual catalog comparison sample sizes; unconditional interruption cells use their declared n (no substitution by smoke preset), and the accepted conditional comparison uses total60 independent conditional-environment continuations,30per arm. Required n240 cases remain required wherever the manifest calls for them. No new production study sample size or reduction in pilot repetitions is authorized. Keep source-shift-scale pilots completely separate.

For arm/component c let Y_j be its indicator mean in pilot trial j, J=1000. Define S_c = sample SD(Y_1,...,Y_J), the empirical sampling SD of exactly that matched per-arm estimator. Retain mean, S_c, each trial's plug-in SE (including zeros) and the within-/cross-arm covariance. Estimate uncertainty of S_c by delta method: u_j=(Y_j - mean(Y))^2; MCSE(S_c) = sample SD(u_j)/(2*S_c*sqrt(J)). This is an explicitly labeled large-sample pilot approximation, not an exact confidence guarantee. Require S_c>0 and finite MCSE; define lower binding L_c=S_c-1.645*MCSE(S_c), requiring L_c>0. If all event counts are zero/one, S_c=0 and this pilot is unresolved; do not remove those trials or supply a floor. The minimum over all required matched configurations' positive L_c supplies S_min; any required nonpositive/undefined L_c blocks the shared binding. Later actual smaller matched sampling SE tightens it. A later genuinely zero target SE still requires analytic truth or unresolved status.

For unconditional IID Bernoulli arms, additionally compare S_c with sqrt(p_hat*(1-p_hat)/n_arm) using the pooled independent pilot roster. Retain a95%binomial interval [l,u] for p and the conservative analytic SE lower bound sqrt(min(l*(1-l),u*(1-u))/n_arm); include that positive lower bound in the minimum. A zero lower bound is unresolved. Material disagreement between empirical and analytic sampling dispersion requires investigation, not choosing a looser gate. Conditional pilots retain the approved independent-filter refinement/stability evidence: finite-filter variability cannot be used to inflate S_min and relax truth precision. Freeze only after the accepted two-refinement check at the final epsilon is met; provisional values can guide work but cannot admit computed truth.

This permits an executable nonzero rare-event path without treating an individual zero-count trial as zero population variance. Illustration only, not a result: at p=.02 and n_arm=30, the true Bernoulli-mean SE is sqrt(.02*.98/30)≈.0256 while a single trial has zero events with probability .98^30≈.545. Across1,000independent trials, empirical dispersion and a pooled bound can be informative despite many zero-count trials. At lower rates they may not be; the retained1,000-trial pilot/cap can honestly remain unresolved. Further pilot size, method or cap requires reviewed protocol revision, not an automatic retry-until-pass rule. This is numerical precision, not rare-event safety assurance.

